# Goal 13: Fix log1pf — wrong value at -1

## Function
`log1pf` (float)

## Source files
- C: /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathf/log1pf.c
- Rust: /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s3/src/mathf.rs

## Problem
log1pf(-1) = -0x1p+1 (-2.0, Rust) vs -inf (C)

log(1 + (-1)) = log(0) = -infinity. The Rust implementation returns -2 instead of -inf, indicating the special case for x == -1 (pole at zero) is not handled correctly.

## What needs to change
Compare Rust log1pf against C log1pf.c. Add or fix the special case: when x == -1.0f, return -INFINITY. The C code likely checks for this explicitly.

## Success Criteria
- `log1pf -0x1p+0` = `-inf` (bitwise exact)
- All other log1pf tests continue to pass
